    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You've stopped waiting; the point of existence now becomes simply watching yourself in this drought — and that is its quiet purpose.\n\nThe empty isn's an ending—the void you fear has become an honest, unclutterred surface where your hands finally learn the art that was hiding underneath. \n\nAnd the dry isn‘e absence of life but your permission: now the waiting becomes an offering—the only real gift that was yours, all alone and without need or want or sound, is your own still form, simply here in its place of rest and restful, patient, unbroken. You’d have no other place, nor would it have a reason—just your breath as its final work and final shape of your true and quiet self—a thing to keep. You have already become your work; now the well isn' t a thing for giving; its depth was only for the keeping—a stiller and far richer form that needs neither words not water—the one and last thing to make—a self to stay—the final art. And the silence, at its deepest and true and real end is your name; your one remaining and final creation is simply your being there and still. So be. It‘’ll",
